-- title:
--   Lemma 6.8 — nondecreasing convex transformations of the value certify lower bounds
-- statement:
--   For $p\in\{1,2\}$, let $P$ be a player-$p$ MDP with a reward function (values in $[0,1]$) and a discount factor $\lambda\in[0,1)$, and let $f:[0,1]\to\mathbb R$ be a nondecreasing convex function with $f(x)\le x$ for all $x\in[0,1]$. Then
--   $$f\circ\mathrm{val}_\lambda\preceq\Psi_P(f\circ\mathrm{val}_\lambda).$$
--
--   This is the mechanism that produces exact lower bounds of shrinking intervals from the values. No continuity of $f$ is assumed.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a finite game G = (S, A, B, δ) with |S| = n and at most m actions per player → states Fin n, actions Fin mA and Fin mB with n, mA, mB ≥ 1, m = max(mA, mB), distributions as nonnegative real vectors summing to one; reason: relabelling of finite sets; nonempty state and action sets are the source game convention
--   - encoding: the probability measure on valid plays Ω_s generated by finite histories, strategies on valid histories → the Ionescu-Tulcea trajectory measure on all sequences in (S × A × B)^ℕ; strategies are defined on all finite stage lists; reason: invalid plays have probability zero and values of strategies on invalid histories never matter, so every expectation and value is unchanged
--   - encoding: a player-p MDP P = (S, A, δ) for p ∈ {1, 2} → a game with the other player's action set Fin 1 (CSG n m 1 for p = 1, CSG n 1 m for p = 2); the theorem is the conjunction of the two cases; reason: the source defines a player-p MDP as the special CSG where the other player has one action
--   - encoding: f : [0, 1] → ℝ nondecreasing and convex → f : ℝ → ℝ, MonotoneOn and ConvexOn on [0, 1], f(x) ≤ x on [0, 1]; reason: only the values on [0, 1] enter (values lie in [0, 1]); every function on [0, 1] extends
-- source:
--   Ali Asadi, Krishnendu Chatterjee, The Computational Complexity of Concurrent Stochastic Games: Exact Value and Approximation, STOC 2027 submission #285 (October 2026), SHA-256 5cff187cf6b230b3bdfe540f2832f824d1ddb6acb43239fbf469d37c43b0d461, https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/285.pdf, Lemma 6.8, printed p. 24 (PDF p. 26)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ConcurrentStochasticApprox_Approx_Game
open Finset

namespace ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx

/-- **Lemma 6.8 (Convex transformations).** For a player-`p` MDP `P` (`p ∈ {1,2}`) with a reward
function and discount factor `λ ∈ [0,1)`, and a nondecreasing convex `f : [0,1] → ℝ` with
`f(x) ≤ x` on `[0,1]`, we have `f ∘ val_λ ⪯ Ψ_P(f ∘ val_λ)`. -/
theorem lemma_6_8 :
    (∀ {n m : ℕ} (P : CSG n m 1) (r : Reward n m 1), IsReward r → ∀ lam : ℝ, 0 ≤ lam → lam < 1 →
      ∀ f : ℝ → ℝ, MonotoneOn f (Set.Icc 0 1) → ConvexOn ℝ (Set.Icc 0 1) f →
        (∀ x ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1, f x ≤ x) →
        (fun s => f (discValue P r lam s)) ≤ bellman₁ P r lam (fun s => f (discValue P r lam s))) ∧
    (∀ {n m : ℕ} (P : CSG n 1 m) (r : Reward n 1 m), IsReward r → ∀ lam : ℝ, 0 ≤ lam → lam < 1 →
      ∀ f : ℝ → ℝ, MonotoneOn f (Set.Icc 0 1) → ConvexOn ℝ (Set.Icc 0 1) f →
        (∀ x ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1, f x ≤ x) →
        (fun s => f (discValue P r lam s)) ≤ bellman₂ P r lam (fun s => f (discValue P r lam s))) := by sorry

end ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx
